# The infinite-pm/ipm-tools ref that release.yml builds the bundled ipm-rpc
# server from. Blank lines and #-comments ignored; one ref (tag, branch or SHA).
#
# ci.yml deliberately does NOT read this — it builds against ipm-tools main so
# palette drift and API breaks surface on the next push, not at release time.
# Releases pin, so a release is reproducible from its own tag; the resolved SHA
# is recorded in the release notes either way.
#
# This must name a ref that EXISTS in infinite-pm/ipm-tools: preflight resolves
# it before anything is built, so a release fails fast on a typo or on a tag
# that was never pushed.
v0.4.2
